WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.872
Before we change any data, we should always check it first.

2
00:00:04.872 --> 00:00:10.055
In this lesson, you will learn to count values with table, remove rows safely,

3
00:00:10.055 --> 00:00:15.238
and avoid one tiny mistake, a missing comma, that can change your data in

4
00:00:15.238 --> 00:00:17.459
a way you did not expect.

5
00:00:17.459 --> 00:00:18.940
Let's be careful together.

6
00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:22.085
First, some tidying.

7
00:00:22.085 --> 00:00:28.940
I remove the extra tables we made, Demographic one and Main, so the Environment is clear.

8
00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:41.790
Under the note, to bring changes in a single or more cells, I start with table.

9
00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:45.440
Table of Demographic, dollar sign, Sex of household head.

10
00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:49.309
The dollar sign picks one column from a table.

11
00:00:49.309 --> 00:00:51.622
Run it, and the console shows:

12
00:00:51.622 --> 00:00:54.320
Female one, Male three hundred fifty one.

13
00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:16.877
Let's view the table.

14
00:01:16.877 --> 00:01:21.609
In row one, the household head is female, a widow from Khost.

15
00:01:21.609 --> 00:01:23.580
Let's practice removing that row.

16
00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:40.420
I type Demographic, open square bracket, minus one, close bracket. But look:

17
00:01:40.420 --> 00:01:42.127
I forgot the comma!

18
00:01:42.127 --> 00:01:47.247
Without the comma, R removed the first column, not the first row.

19
00:01:47.247 --> 00:01:51.940
Only one observation of three variables is shown. Something is wrong.

20
00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:05.230
So I recreate the table, and this time I write minus one, then a comma.

21
00:02:05.230 --> 00:02:07.860
Now R knows the one is a row.

22
00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:29.472
Run it, and the table has three hundred fifty one rows.

23
00:02:29.472 --> 00:02:33.264
Table now shows Male three hundred fifty, and no female.

24
00:02:33.264 --> 00:02:35.160
Exactly one row is gone.

25
00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:55.443
Every time you remove a row, run table again, and check that the numbers

26
00:02:55.443 --> 00:02:57.280
changed the way you expected.

27
00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:12.955
Here I remove row one hundred twelve.

28
00:03:12.955 --> 00:03:15.609
Three hundred forty eight rows are left.

29
00:03:15.609 --> 00:03:17.126
Check, change, check again.

30
00:03:17.126 --> 00:03:20.160
That is a very good habit. Well done!

